   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/r1334-opus-r2, round 2) : APPROVE** — tête 667b9d0\n\nNo findings.\n\nThe round 1 finding is fixed. In `App/SwiftHFR/Notifications/MPBackgroundCheck.swift:14` the doc comment is back to its original wording, and the `legacyText` value is still « Tu as un nouveau message privé ». `git diff 5957c31 667b9d0` changes only that one line, so the rest of the diff is the same as in round 1.\n\nRe-checked:\n- **Strings still in « vous »:** none left in `App/SwiftHFR`. I searched string literals, the Info.plist usage keys in `project.pbxproj` and imperatives ending in -ez. The only -ez hit is « Allez on remballe » (`NoelPackingLayer.swift`), a « on » interjection, so it is fine. Every « vous / votre » left in `Packages/HFRKit` is HFR server text used for matching (`HopResponseParser`, `LoginResponse`, `PollVoteFlow`, `PostingAction`), and the PR touches no file under `Packages/`, which is correct.\n- **Tests against source:** the tests that still contain « Votre … » are server confirmations (`ConfirmationAutoDismissTests`, `ComposerTestSupport`, `NewMessageComposerTests`, `NewTopicComposerTests`, `ReplyEntryTests`), so they are correct. Every new string literal added in the tests diff has a match in `App/SwiftHFR`. The suffixes « renvoie le message. » and « renvoie le sujet. » come from the interpolation `renvoie \\(what).` at `ComposerMessages.swift:21`. No added line mixes « tu » and « vous ».\n\n**Vérifié**\n- `git worktree add` at 667b9d0.\n- `git diff --stat 5957c31 667b9d0`: one line.\n- `swiftlint lint --strict --quiet` on the 85 changed Swift files: exit 0, no output.\n- `swiftc -parse` on each changed Swift file: no errors.\n- Character lengths (not bytes) of the four longest lines (`ComposerMessages.swift:148,187`, `ReaderAlertFlow.swift:5`, `SmileyPickerModel.swift:155`): all ≤ 140, and none longer than on the base.\n- The greps above. The app was not built and the app tests were not run (Linux).\n\nReviewer model: 