   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/r1334-opus-r3, round 3): APPROVE** — tête 15b9f33\n\nNo findings.\n\n1. **Merge.** `git show --remerge-diff 15b9f33` is empty. The merge of `f4cb0d9` (which is `origin/dev-swift`) adds nothing to the automatic result, so the APPROVE given on 667b9d0 still applies.\n2. **New strings from #1333, #1335, #1336 and #1338.** I checked every user-facing line added under `App/SwiftHFR` between 667b9d0 and 15b9f33. None uses « vous » and none mixes « tu » and « vous ». Some examples:\n   - the `AlertTitles` set, for example « Ajout impossible », « Activer le stockage MP ? », « Publier sur Alertes Qualitay ? »;\n   - the VoiceOver labels « Conversation de groupe » and « Nouvelle »;\n   - « \\(pseudo) est déjà dans la liste. ».\n\n   The repo-wide search was case-insensitive, for `vous`, `votre` and `vos` and for `-ez` imperatives in quoted strings in `App/SwiftHFR` and `App/SwiftHFRTests`. Its only matches in user strings are allowed:\n   - HFR server texts in test inputs (`MarkUnreadTests.swift:99`, `TopicListModelTests.swift:96-102`, `TopicListLoggedOutTests.swift:24`);\n   - « Rendez-vous », a test topic title (`NewMessageComposerTests.swift`, `MessageComposerEntryTests.swift`);\n   - HFR's charter, served as is (`Resources/static-charter.html`);\n   - the generated `changelog-v1.json`, which is out of scope.\n   - « Allez on remballe » (`NoelPackingLayer.swift:58,91`) is the interjection « allez », not a « vous » imperative.\n3. **Tests vs sources.** I matched every string literal added to the tests by the merge against `App/SwiftHFR`. The ones absent from the code are the old titles the tests check are gone (« Action impossible », « Service de GIF », « Hébergeur d'images »), test names and fixture URLs. No test asserts a string the PR changed.\n\n**Vérifié**:\n- `git show --remerge-diff 15b9f33`: empty.\n- The searches above, over the files at 15b9f33 and over the diff 667b9d0..15b9f33 under `App/`.\n- `swiftlint lint --strict --quiet` on the 85 Swift files added or changed vs `origin/dev-swift` (f4cb0d9): exit 0.\n- `swiftc -parse` on the same files: exit 0.\n- Not run: the app-hosted tests (Linux session; CI decides).\n\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (cloud/r1334-opus-r3).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
